# Generated by scripts/celegans_fate_reads.py (genomeos.organism.fate_rules): terminal fates from
# the measured factors (Ma et al. 2021), read by the runtime as `F.exposure(lineage)` — minutes carried
# along the lineage window, threshold 15, integrated by the Body itself (BIOLANG-v0.4-ECONOMY.md §7.2a).
# threshold 15 min = one AB cell cycle at 20 C (Sulston et al. 1983, Dev Biol 100:64), so the read is 'carried along the lineage path across at least one division'; 1 to 30 min give the identical program and score, and the cited rules alone are flat to 60 min (scripts/celegans_fate_reads.py).
# Imported after the lineage program, so a factor rule overrides the observed fate of a terminal
# cell and the lookup stays the fallback. Precedence is the `priority` of each decision (first
# rule highest; the lookup has 0) under `regime { fates: first }`, declared by the importer.
module organism.celegans.fates
import cell_types.bio

decision factor_fate_00 { action: differentiate; when: cell_type = Coelomocyte|Epithelium|Excretory|Gland|GliaSheath|GliaSocket|Hypodermis|Intestine|Mesoderm|Muscle|Neuron|Other|PharyngealMarginal|Rectal|Reproductive|TailSpike|Valve, stage = Cleavage|Gastrulation|Morphogenesis, ELT-2.exposure(lineage) >= 15; to: Intestine; priority: 24; evidence: experimental "Fukushige et al. 1998, Dev Biol 198:286; Sommermann et al. 2010, Dev Biol 347:154; read as exposure over the lineage window, threshold 15 min = one AB cell cycle at 20 C (Sulston et al. 1983, Dev Biol 100:64), so the read is 'carried along the lineage path across at least one division'; 1 to 30 min give the identical program and score, and the cited rules alone are flat to 60 min (scripts/celegans_fate_reads.py); factors Ma et al. 2021, Nat Methods 18:893 (Zenodo 4737593)"; confidence: 0.8 }
